-- ============================================================================
-- DR10 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Stimulation Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the chain from a pumped schedule to a number a
-- reservoir engineer can use. The pad and the ramp, the pack that is left
-- behind, its conductivity, and the fracture expressed as a skin.
--
-- THE HEADLINE, AND IT IS DERIVED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. The engine carries 1.6
-- as the unified fracture design optimum, a published constant. A golden
-- section search on the engine's OWN Cinco-Ley pseudo-skin, at fixed proppant
-- volume, has no knowledge of that constant and lands at 1.6363280591 anyway,
-- a ratio of 1.0227. A constant you can rederive from an independent route is
-- a RESULT; one you can only quote is a CONVENTION. The search lives in the
-- teaching lab and is asserted in its vitest file, so an edit that broke the f
-- function would drift it off 1.6 and the suite would say so. The tier also
-- teaches why the continuous search is trustworthy and the discrete grid is
-- not: a grid returns the best row it happened to include.
--
-- THE TRAP, AND IT IS THE MOST VALUABLE LESSON IN THE COURSE. The pad fraction
-- is (1 minus the efficiency) divided by (1 PLUS the efficiency), and NOT one
-- minus the efficiency. The naive form is always the larger, because dividing
-- by one plus eta can only shrink the answer, so the error is always TOO MUCH
-- PAD and never too little, which shortens the fracture and wastes the job.
-- The error is not monotonic: it vanishes at both ends of the efficiency range
-- and peaks in the middle, at eta = sqrt(2) - 1 with the exact value
-- 3 - 2*sqrt(2). A first draft of the lab's test asserted it grew as
-- efficiency fell, and the engine disagreed.
--
-- WHAT THE CHAIN LOSES AT EVERY LINK, which is the idea m06 closes on: the pad
-- to leakoff, the pack to porosity and to the damage factor, the length to
-- thinning at fixed proppant volume. The propped width that survives is a
-- small fraction of the width that was created, and the difference is simply
-- what closed.
-- ============================================================================

values ('stimulation', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-pad-and-the-ramp","title":"The Pad and the Ramp","lesson_keys":["l01-why-a-pad-at-all","l02-the-nolte-exponent","l03-the-ramp","l04-the-pad-fraction-trap"]},{"key":"m02-from-slurry-to-pack","title":"From Slurry to Pack","lesson_keys":["l01-the-placed-mass","l02-areal-concentration","l03-propped-width","l04-pack-porosity","l05-the-damage-factor"]},{"key":"m03-conductivity","title":"Conductivity","lesson_keys":["l01-conductivity-is-a-product","l02-dimensionless-conductivity","l03-closure-stress-crushes","l04-retained-permeability","l05-what-conductivity-buys"]},{"key":"m04-the-fracture-as-a-skin","title":"The Fracture as a Skin","lesson_keys":["l01-cinco-ley-and-samaniego","l02-the-f-function","l03-the-pseudo-skin","l04-the-effective-wellbore-radius","l05-a-frac-is-not-a-bigger-hole"]},{"key":"m05-the-unified-design-optimum","title":"The Unified Design Optimum","lesson_keys":["l01-the-one-point-six-result","l02-trading-length-against-width","l03-reading-a-design-off-the-optimum","l04-what-the-optimum-assumes"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
